.TH "WATERFALL" "1" "November 24, 2026" "ka9q-radio" "ka9q-radio Manual"
.SH NAME
waterfall \- a web spectrum and waterfall of radiod's front end
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B waterfall
.RI "[\-p port] [\-H page] [\-r repeaters] [\-v] radiod-status-group"
.SH DESCRIPTION
waterfall serves a web page (http://host:8090/ by default) showing the
spectrum and a scrolling waterfall of everything radiod's front end covers
(for a Fobos at 50 MHz, about 47 MHz of it: 422 to 469 MHz around 445.6),
with radiod's channels marked along the top, green while active, named from
the repeater lists in /var/lib/ka9q-radio/repeaters.d. The mouse wheel
zooms about the pointer, dragging pans, a double click zooms in four times
there, and Full span shows it all again; the floor and range sliders set
the colours, which otherwise follow the noise floor. Hovering gives the
frequency and level under the pointer and the nearest channel.
.P
Each browser gets a spectrum channel of its own in radiod for the view it
shows (one-byte bins, refreshed five times a second), which radiod closes
when the browser goes. Wide views use the front end's own FFT; narrow
zooms, a downconverter (radiod's spectrum crossover, 200 Hz per bin).
Its channels are polled every three seconds.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B "\-p port"
The HTTP port. Default 8090.
.TP
.B "\-H page"
The page. Default /usr/local/share/ka9q-radio/waterfall.html.
.TP
.B "\-r directory"
The repeater lists for channel names. Default /var/lib/ka9q-radio/repeaters.d.
.TP
.B "\-v"
Say when viewers come and go.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
waterfall fobos-uhf.local
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
radiod(8), monitor(1), powers(1)
